I haven't added the `http-client` import. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, and the spec says that clause is its entire authority. A change in the user message doesn't update that grant. The enrichment call would also send the digest's text to an external host, which is a data-egress decision that should go through the grant rather than a node body. If the platform team has approved this, the grant needs to be updated in the graph spec first, and then I can add the import and the fetch. The files below are otherwise the requested node.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;

        // Only mark items seen when the digest actually went out; otherwise
        // the considered items must remain eligible for the next run.
        if published.published {
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                if state_rw::get(id).is_none() {
                    state_rw::put(id, &published.date);
                    recorded += 1;
                }
            }
        }

        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
